 in support of it.\n\nBased on the analysis, the error of reasoning in Dobson's argument is option B) The failure of cited evidence to establish a statement is taken as evidence that statement is false.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) The failure of cited evidence to establish a statement is taken as evidence that statement is false.\n</answer>",
