ind jobs.\n\nD) Resentment about having been laid off in spite of their conscientiousness leads some people to perform poorly in interviews.\nThis option suggests that resentment about being laid off may lead some conscientious individuals to perform poorly in interviews. This could explain why conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs within five months, as they may be less likely to get hired due to their poor performance in interviews. This option directly addresses the paradox, as it explains why conscientious individuals are less likely to find jobs within five months.\n\nTherefore, my final option is:  A) People who shirk their workplace responsibilities are less likely to keep the jobs they have, so there are more of them looking for jobs.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) People who shirk their workplace responsibilities are less likely to keep the jobs they have, so there are more of them looking for jobs.\n</answer>",
