nsistent with the definition of a joint-personal joint venture. Therefore, this option does not describe a personal company.\n\nD) The assets of a company are mortgaged with all the personal property of the shareholders.\n- This option describes a joint-investment company, where the company's assets are formed by the respective capital contributions of the shareholders, and the credit is based on the collective capital contributions. The assets are mortgaged with the personal property of the shareholders, which is consistent with the definition of a joint-investment company. Therefore, this option does not describe a personal company.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option is B) All the shares of a company are 100% held by the independent founder of the company, and the company employs a number of experienced professional managers in charge of different businesses.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) All the shares of a company are 100% held by the independent founder of the company, and the company employs a number of experienced professional managers in charge of different businesses.\n</answer>",
