, if accurate, would provide support for the main conclusion, and the second boldface portion is the main conclusion. However, the second boldface portion is not the main conclusion but a conclusion drawn from the prediction.\n\nD) The first is a prediction that, if accurate, would provide support for the main conclusion of the argument; the second is that main conclusion.\n   - This option suggests that the first boldface portion is a prediction that, if accurate, would provide support for the main conclusion, and the second boldface portion is the main conclusion. This fits the context of the argument perfectly.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) The first is a prediction that, if accurate, would provide support for the main conclusion of the argument; the second is that main conclusion.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) The first is a prediction that, if accurate, would provide support for the main conclusion of the argument; the second is that main conclusion.\n</answer>",
