th the context, as each transition from wood to coal, then to oil and natural gas involves a decrease in carbon and an increase in hydrogen.\n\n   - Option B: This option states that if the second stage of a process is completed more quickly than the first stage, the third stage will also be completed more quickly than the second stage. However, this does not relate to the context, as it does not describe a series of changes or a decrease/increase of attributes.\n\n   - Option C: This option suggests that if two desirable attributes belong to a useful substance, the most useful form of that substance will have those two attributes in equal amounts. While this may be true in some cases, it does not necessarily apply to the context, as the context does not mention any specific desirable attributes or their equal amounts.\n\n   - Option D: This option states that if one substance is better for a certain purpose than another substance, the best substance for that purpose is one that includes all attributes of the first substance and none of the attributes of the second substance. This does not align with the context, as it does not describe a series of changes or a decrease/increase of attributes.\n\n8. Based on the analysis, the correct answer is Option A, as it accurately describes the pattern observed in the context.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) If each step in a series of changes involves a decrease of one attribute of the thing undergoing the change and an increase of another, the series will terminate with the first attribute eliminated and only the second attribute present.\n</answer>",
