oncludes that we should ensure that internet users have at least as much freedom of expression as did people speaking in the public square. This implies that a public forum can lose effectiveness as a tool of democracy if participants cannot discuss issues freely.\n\nTherefore, the correct assumption required by the argument is: D) A public forum can lose effectiveness as a tool of democracy if participants cannot discuss issues freely.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) A public forum can lose effectiveness as a tool of democracy if participants cannot discuss issues freely.\n</answer>",
