ons to which one is opposed. This option suggests that the argument does not consider the challenge of creating persuasive arguments against opposing positions, which is a crucial aspect of the argument.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC) Fails to account for the difficulty of coming up with charitable formulations of positions to which one is opposed.\n</answer>",
