ged the gap between China's cultural heritage and global audiences, the most accurate option is **A) It's national, it's world**. This option aligns with the context's message that national works can indeed achieve world recognition, contrary to the other options which either overstate or understate the relationship between national and world recognition.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) It's national, it's world\n</answer>",
