at Jupiter's gravity pushed them into smaller orbits, but did not drive them out of the solar system. This is inconsistent with the second assertion, as it implies that Jupiter's gravity did not drive them out of the solar system.\n   d) This option states that Jupiter's gravitational pull neither pushed them into smaller orbits nor drove them out of the solar system. This is inconsistent with both assertions, as it implies that Jupiter's gravity did not have any effect on the movement of the planets.\n\n6. Based on the analysis, the only option that can be inferred if only one of the above two assertions is true is option B: Jupiter's gravity did not push them into smaller orbits, but drove them out of the solar system. This is consistent with the second assertion, but not necessarily with the first assertion.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) Jupiter's gravity did not push them into smaller orbits, but drove them out of the solar system.\n</answer>",
