      "text": " A. \n<think>\nTo determine which option is not subject to national pricing, let's analyze each option step by step:\n\nA) A well-known shopping mall has newly imported a batch of high-end cashmere sweaters. For the credibility of the shopping mall, the boss decided to sell the new products at a 30% discount in the first three days of the market.\n\nThis option involves a discount on the price of the cashmere sweaters, which is a pricing strategy by the mall. However, it is not a government-mandated pricing policy. Therefore, this option is not subject to national pricing.\n\nB) On the eve of the start of school in the spring of 2005, the education bureau of a certain city issued a notice about the tuition and miscellaneous fees of various schools in the new semester, and asked the school to announce it.\n\nThis option involves a notice issued by the education bureau regarding tuition and miscellaneous fees for schools. This is a government-mandated pricing policy, as it sets the fees for schools. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing.\n\nC) On the eve of the spring festival, in order to safeguard the interests of the general public and stabilize the order of the holiday market, the municipal price bureau approved and announced the maximum prices of some commodities such as poultry eggs, vegetables, and aquatic products.\n\nThis option involves the municipal price bureau approving and announcing maximum prices for certain commodities during the spring festival. This is a government-mandated pricing policy, as it sets the maximum prices for these commodities. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing.\n\nD) The charging standards for buses in Nanjing are clearly: 1 yuan per ride for ordinary unmanned ticket vending vehicles, 2 yuan per ride for air-conditioned unmanned ticket vending vehicles, and 20% off for passengers with bus cards.\n\nThis option involves charging standards for buses in Nanjing, which are clearly defined. This is a government-mandated pricing policy, as it sets the charging standards for buses. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing.\n\nBased on the analysis, the option that is not subject to national pricing is A) A well-known shopping mall has newly imported a batch of high-end cashmere sweaters. For the credibility of the shopping mall, the boss decided to sell the new products at a 30% discount in the first three days of the market.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) A well-known shopping mall has newly imported a batch of high-end cashmere sweaters. For the credibility of the shopping mall, the boss decided to sell the new products at a 30% discount in the first three days of the market.\n</answer>",
