ument, as it uses the similarity of Comrade Bethune's attributes to draw a conclusion about his character.\n\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper.\n- This option compares silver and copper based on their electrical conductivity. It concludes that silver is more suitable for conductive materials than copper based on their resistivity. This is not an analogical argument, as it does not involve a comparison of two objects based on shared attributes to draw a conclusion about another attribute.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option that belongs to an analogical argument is B) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation.\n</answer>",
