he future of 3D movies is uncertain. While this is true, it does not directly address the concern about the replacement of live-action performances by computer-generated images and animations. Therefore, this option does not reduce the actor's worries.\n\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director - This statement suggests that the heart and emotion of the actor are the only factors that matter in expressing the film story, and the preferences of the director do not influence the form of expression. This statement directly addresses the concern about the replacement of live-action performances by computer-generated images and animations. If the film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, then the actor's performances will still be crucial in conveying the story, regardless of whether the characters are computer-generated or live-action. Therefore, this option can most reduce the actor's worries.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) The film story can only be expressed by the heart and emotion of the actor, and its form of expression has nothing to do with the preferences of the director.\n</answer>",
