messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInternational economic law is the general term of international law and domestic law that regulate the relationship between countries, international organizations, legal persons and natural persons engaged in transnational economic exchanges.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following statements is wrong?\n# Options:\nA) International economic law includes both international law and domestic law.\nB) Transnational marriage does not belong to the object regulated by international economic law.\nC) International economic law contains agreements between states on maritime territorial delimitation.\nD) The subjects of transnational economic exchanges include states, international organizations, legal persons and natural persons.', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
