messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWe cannot simply think that the editors of the lexicon are wrong. They will not make changes to the usage of the vocabulary randomly, and must have been carefully researched. However, the lexicographers cannot ignore a basic fact and the basic requirements derived from it : Spoken and written languages are commonly used by the broad masses of the people and have a very broad social nature. Therefore, the standardization of spoken and written languages cannot be carried out in the ivory tower, but must follow the mass line.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the basic requirements in this passage?\n# Options:\nA) The lexicographer cannot change the usage of the vocabulary at will\nB) The lexicographer should be familiar with the specific process of lexicography\nC) Standardization of spoken and written languages must serve the broad masses of people\nD) The standardization of spoken and written language should be decided by the broad masses of people', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
