ears rather than decades or hundreds of years, which is difficult to be connected with our rapidly changing modern climate conditions.\n- This option suggests that climate cooling lasts for more than millions of years, which contradicts the context provided, which mentions that the new ocean basins around Africa, South America, and Europe began to expand, creating new spaces. Therefore, this option does not support the scientists' judgment.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is B) Global warming will lead to a crisis of marine life. scientists found that a similar crisis had occurred in marine life during the global cooling period 260000 years ago.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) Global warming will lead to a crisis of marine life. scientists found that a similar crisis had occurred in marine life during the global cooling period 260000 years ago.\n</answer>",
