be treated effectively by the methods of alternative medicine.\n- This statement can be inferred from the context. The context states that alternative medicine is free of side effects because it does not have any effects at all. This implies that alternative medicine is a safe and effective option for those who cannot tolerate the side effects of orthodox medicine. Therefore, it is possible that alternative medicine can treat some trivial illnesses effectively.\n\nD) Practitioners of alternative medicine are acting in bad faith.\n- This statement cannot be inferred from the context. The context only mentions that alternative medicine is free of side effects because it does not have any effects at all. It does not provide any information about the motives or actions of practitioners of alternative medicine.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is C) There are some trivial illnesses that can be treated effectively by the methods of alternative medicine.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC) There are some trivial illnesses that can be treated effectively by the methods of alternative medicine.\n</answer>",
