 albinism are unusually susceptible to sunburn and other sun-related ailments.\n\n7. Option D states that when a non-albino person gets sunburn, the amount of melanin produced by that person decreases. This is not supported by the context, as the context does not mention any changes in melanin production in response to sunburn.\n\nBased on the analysis, the most accurate conclusion supported by the given context is option A: In humans, melanin plays a role in protecting the skin from developing sunburn and other sun-related ailments.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) In humans, melanin plays a role in protecting the skin from developing sunburn and other sun-related ailments.\n</answer>",
