on B is the most appropriate choice because it directly addresses the principle that those who benefit from an economic service should bear the costs of that service. This aligns with the argument that depositors benefit from the insurance and should therefore bear the cost.\n\nTherefore, my final answer is: B) The people who stand to benefit from an economic service should always be made to bear the costs of that service.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) The people who stand to benefit from an economic service should always be made to bear the costs of that service.\n</answer>",
