involves adding excessive food coloring to a candy produced, which is a food product. However, the fact that long-term consumption would cause harm to human health is not relevant to the crime of producing and selling toxic or harmful food. Therefore, this option does not constitute the crime of producing and selling toxic or harmful food.\n\nBased on the analysis, options A and B both involve mixing toxic or harmful non-food raw materials in food, which constitutes the crime of producing and selling toxic or harmful food. Therefore, the correct options are A and B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA and B\n</answer>",
