n advance by one party to the contract to the other party. This meets the definition of a deposit because it was paid in advance and was used to guarantee the performance of the contract.\n\nC) Changhai company signed a contract with zhiming oil factory for the production and marketing of salad oil. the contract stipulates that zhiming oil factory should supply 80 tons of high-quality salad oil to changhai company within 5 months after the signing of the contract. during this period, zhiming oil factory had a mechanical accident, resulting in the shutdown of the factory for 3 months. due to the failure to deliver on time, zhiming oil factory paid 30,000 yuan to changhai company according to the contract.\n\nIn this case, zhiming oil factory paid 30,000 yuan to changhai company, which is a certain amount paid in advance by one party to the contract to the other party. This meets the definition of a deposit because it was paid in advance and was used to guarantee the performance of the contract.\n\nD) At an order meeting, the deputy general manager of aetna trading company signed a contract for the purchase and sale of flax silk with a printing and dyeing factory, with a total contract amount of 7.8 million yuan. according to the agreement between the two sides, the printing and dyeing factory should pay aetna trading company 1.56 million yuan according to 20% of the contract amount as a good faith to perform the contract, but the printing and dyeing factory was very short of funds, so it couldn't get so much money at the moment, so it pieced together to pay 1 million yuan.\n\nIn this case, the printing and dyeing factory paid 1 million yuan to aetna trading company, which is a certain amount paid in advance by one party to the contract to the other party. This meets the definition of a deposit because it was paid in advance and was used to guarantee the performance of the contract.\n\nBased on the analysis, options B, C, and D all meet the definition of a deposit. However, since the question asks for the correct option, I will choose option B as the answer.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) Fenghua company in qiqihar ordered 38 tons of beef from shenda company in inner mongolia. due to the large sales, shenda is a small company, and its working capital is not enough, so it is difficult to acquire the required amount of beef. considering the actual situation of shenda company, fenghua company paid 50,000 yuan in advance to shenda company in order to make the intention as soon as possible.\n</answer>",
