one mentioned, cannot be thought unlikely to occur over the long run. This implies that a serious accident at a nuclear power plant is not improbable, as everyday events can lead to accidents.\n\nBased on the analysis, the most strongly supported statement by the given information is option D: If nuclear power plants continue in operation, a serious accident at such a plant is not improbable.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) If nuclear power plants continue in operation, a serious accident at such a plant is not improbable.\n</answer>",
