han previously thought. This implies that the total amount of light reflected from the comet is actually higher than previously thought, not lower. Therefore, this option is not supported by the information provided.\n\nD) Scientists need more information before they can make a good estimate of the mass of Halley's comet.\n- This option suggests that scientists require additional information to accurately estimate the mass of Halley's comet. However, the given information provides new insights into the reflective properties of Halley's comet's material, which can help improve the accuracy of mass estimates. Therefore, this option is not supported by the information provided.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is B) Previous estimates of the mass of Halley's comet which were based on its brightness were too low.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) Previous estimates of the mass of Halley's comet which were based on its brightness were too low.\n</answer>",
