on is the dietary source of virtually all of the glucose (a type of sugar) that reaches that person's bloodstream.\"\n\nBased on the analysis, option B provides the best explanation for coffee's effect on blood-glucose levels as it is described above. Drinking coffee after a meal consisting of several types of foods that themselves rapidly break down into sugars during digestion would lead to a significant increase in blood-glucose levels due to the combined effects of the coffee and the pre-existing sugars from the meal.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) People often drink coffee after a meal consisting of several types of foods that themselves rapidly break down into sugars during digestion.\n</answer>",
