 gives off any gaseous substances that repel mosquitoes.\n- This option suggests that human skin never gives off any gaseous substances that repel mosquitoes. If this were true, it would imply that the additional gaseous substance attracting mosquitoes is not related to any substances that repel mosquitoes. However, the context does not mention anything about substances that repel mosquitoes, so this option is not required for the argument.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct assumption required for the argument is:\n\nA) Mosquitoes are no more successful in finding a bare human arm in darkness than in light.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) Mosquitoes are no more successful in finding a bare human arm in darkness than in light.\n</answer>",
