e Yuan people already had some understanding of the geographical situation of Africa.\n\nC) The Yuan dynasty was the most developed period of maritime traffic in China.\n- This statement is not supported by the context. The context only mentions that the Yuan Dynasty inherited the policy of opening to the outside world in the Tang and Song dynasties, strengthened its political ties with overseas countries, and actively carried out overseas trade economically, but it does not provide information about the development of maritime traffic in China.\n\nD) The most prosperous overseas trade in China in history was the Yuan dynasty.\n- This statement is not supported by the context. The context only mentions that the Yuan Dynasty inherited the policy of opening to the outside world in the Tang and Song dynasties, strengthened its political ties with overseas countries, and actively carried out overseas trade economically, but it does not provide information about the most prosperous overseas trade in China in history.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is B) The western expedition of the Yuan dynasty reached Africa and drew a map accordingly.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB) The western expedition of the Yuan dynasty reached Africa and drew a map accordingly.\n</answer>",
