messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSome TV ads take the same words, repeated many times in order to deepen the audience's impression, so that the audience remember the product to be promoted. In fact, this is unwise.Surveys show that many long-term such advertising businesses. Lately, they've been in economic trouble, with a huge backlog of products. It can be seen that the business not only did not achieve the desired purpose, but also produced a negative effect.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options best emphasizes the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) Although some tv viewers don't care about the same ad being repeated, many viewers feel it's best to take more of the art of advertising into account\nB) Because the audience is with a good tv program after watching an ad, any ad will make the audience impatient\nC) Although the advertising act does not prohibit the same ad word repeatedly, merchants should consider the diverse feelings of different audiences\nD) Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote", '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
