s the subject matter of insurance.\n- This option is inconsistent with the definition of liability insurance because it involves an insured taking their legal liability for damages (in this case, death and disability of their on-the-job employees due to other injury accidents) as the subject matter of insurance, but it does not specify that the insured is taking their legal liability for damages as the subject matter of insurance. Instead, it seems to imply that the insured is taking the responsibility for the death and disability of their on-the-job employees, which is not necessarily the same as taking their legal liability for damages.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) Enterprises, institutions and social organizations take the death and disability of their on-the-job employees due to other injury accidents as the subject matter of insurance.\n</answer>",
