taste of sour food is not perceived. This does not fit the definition of antagonism because the presence of one odorant (sour sambal) does not weaken the taste characteristics of another odorant (sour food). Instead, it seems to have a different effect, which is not related to antagonism.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is D) After eating sour sambal, and then eating sour food, you will not taste the sour taste.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD) After eating sour sambal, and then eating sour food, you will not taste the sour taste.\n</answer>",
